+Independent reviewer found no confirmed blockers, but requested checking native minimum-size layout. Added glassWindowMinimumSizeFitsHostedContent: a real NSHostingView at the window's contentMinSize has fitting height/width within its bounds. It passes, as do the blank-padding mouse click and resizing regressions. Light/graphite native backing colors, appearances, transparent/full-size chrome and standard controls are asserted; the probe's theme update is checked.
+
+The authorized fixture-only executable and hand-made resource bundle were copied to /private/tmp/BatonFixture.app and launched with open --args --review-window (exit 0). No exact-path old fixture process was running (pkill exit 1, no other process targeted). CUA now successfully shows “Baton Fixture Review”, unlike the prior capture failure. Native screenshot visually confirms the light glass/title-bar continuity. Clicking its full-screen control removed normal-window controls and screenshot showed the enlarged full-screen layout. The user changed the fixture while inspection was ongoing; further UI actions were stopped, and latest state was read. No actual real coding app or chat was accessed. Graphite live appearance is not separately observed; native palette tests cover configuration.
